    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The area that is now Lake Norman of Iredell was first settled by Scotch‑Irish and German immigrants in the mid‑1700s before becoming part of the lake’s modern community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitlakenorman.org/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Catawba River, which feeds Lake Norman, has served Native Americans and early settlers for centuries, and its name translates to “people of the river.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://lakenorman.com/the-history-of-lake-norman-from-creation-to-a-thriving-community/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Lake Norman, North Carolina’s largest man‑made lake, was created by a Duke Power Company dam that also supplied hydroelectric power to the surrounding region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://lakenorman.com/the-history-of-lake-norman-from-creation-to-a-thriving-community/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In the mid‑20th century, families from Charlotte packed station wagons to build homes on Lake Norman’s shores, turning the area into a thriving lakeside community.",
